California polls have just closed, but results will take longer to come in. Why does the state take longer to count its votes? We discuss this with our guest, Guy Marzorati, political correspondent at KQED in the Bay Area.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51978c-d80a-11f1-93d9-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-051136-051356-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c51978c-d80a-11f1-93d9-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-051136-051356-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">413de7fa-d80a-11f1-8ebb-0f62c206b6d8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:20:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: "Keeping our fingers crossed" (Leila Meresman)</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-keeping-our-fingers-crossed-leila-meresman</link><description>
Democrats who once saw the political map as an almost impossible lift are now hopeful that a Senate majority is within reach, even though their path runs through several more conservative states. 

 We discuss this with our guest Leila Meresman, spokesperson of Democrats Abroad France says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1609c5de-d807-11f1-b309-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-041245-042303-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1609c5de-d807-11f1-b309-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-041245-042303-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b08caf8-d807-11f1-bb79-4d6858bc38a0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:15:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Democrats celebrate early victories at a watch party in Los Angeles</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-democrats-celebrate-early-victories-at-a-watch-party-in-los-angeles</link><description>
Our correspondent Wassim Cornet reports from a Democratic watch party in Los Angeles where "people are opening bottles of champagne" following the Democrats' first victories in these midterm elections. We also speak with France 24's Jessica Le Masurier, reporting from Detroit, Michigan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdedb0e0-d805-11f1-8606-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-040106-041156-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdedb0e0-d805-11f1-8606-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-040106-041156-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d2e3062c-d805-11f1-92f3-e300cb4f1f81</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 05:12:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Midterms live : Democrats take control of Senate, ending Republican dominance in Washington</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">f9ec8b50-d808-11f1-9335-9f0f349d867e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 04:37:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Midterms live: Texas, Ohio, North and South Carolina... Democrats have already flipped 4 Senate seats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">c5ecdf50-d806-11f1-917f-c5f1ea16841a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 04:18:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Key US Senate results: Democrats win upper chamber with victories in Texas and Iowa</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-key-us-senate-results-democrats-wrest-north-and-south-carolina-from-the-republicans</link><description>
Democrats won control of the Senate in the US midterm elections Tuesday, with initial results showing the party securing shock victories in Texas, Ohio, North and South Carolina, Kansas and Iowa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4d6ce10-c25e-11f1-bca4-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/Senat-etat-midterms-democrates-republicains.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4d6ce10-c25e-11f1-bca4-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/Senat-etat-midterms-democrates-republicains.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6083558a-d7fd-11f1-8495-3164bccaf44a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 03:52:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a4d6ce10-c25e-11f1-bca4-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/Senat-etat-midterms-democrates-republicains.png">© Studio graphique FMM</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: "Voters have become increasingly frustrated with President Trump"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-voters-have-become-increasingly-frustrated-with-president-trump</link><description>
The polls in these midterm elections suggest that "this will either be a good night or a historic night for Democrats". But what is driving this momentum? We discuss this with our guest, Mallory Newall, Senior Vice President at Ipsos.

"We've seen in our polling at Ipsos in recent weeks and months that voters have become increasingly frustrated with President Trump," she says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c941b364-d7fd-11f1-8a7e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-031154-032057-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c941b364-d7fd-11f1-8a7e-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-031154-032057-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdc1cde8-d7fd-11f1-8b9f-bd45a5f6f7df</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 03:50:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US: "Even in places where the Democrats haven't won, the swing towards them has been significant"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-even-in-places-where-the-democrats-haven-t-won-the-swing-towards-them-has-been-significant</link><description>
Tens of millions of Americans cast their vote in the crucial polls that have been pitched as a referendum on Donald Trump's presidency amid anger at surging petrol prices, tariffs and the Iran war. We discuss the first results with France 24's Kethevane Gorjestani and Fraser Jackson. "Even in places where the Democrats haven't won, the swing towards them has been significant", he says.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cff3b34-d7ff-11f1-a646-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-032057-033303-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0cff3b34-d7ff-11f1-a646-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-032057-033303-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11cc6254-d7ff-11f1-9f89-27b5be33e850</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 03:48:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Democratic gains mount in US midterms as Trump faces bruising verdict</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-democratic-gains-mount-in-us-midterms-as-trump-faces-bruising-verdict</link><description>
Democrats notched a string of early victories in US midterm elections Tuesday, flipping a Republican-held Senate seat and making inroads in conservative House districts as President Donald Trump faced the prospect of a bruising election setback. France 24's Douglas Herbert gives us his analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f406606-d7fc-11f1-84c9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-030853-031149-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f406606-d7fc-11f1-84c9-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-030853-031149-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54faad2c-d7fc-11f1-a6ca-4b1093cf14a8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 03:41:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: Georgia Senator Jon Ossoff wins reelection</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-replay-georgia-senator-jon-ossoff-wins-reelection</link><description>
Georgia Senator Jon Ossoff was reelected Tuesday to a second term, holding a key seat for Democrats by defeating Republican Representative Mike Collins in a race that catapulted the Senate’s youngest member to the forefront of his party’s national stars as it looks to stymie President Donald Trump in his final years in the White House.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b38b5bd6-d7ff-11f1-8783-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-033315-034435-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b38b5bd6-d7ff-11f1-8783-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-033315-034435-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b829bbe2-d7ff-11f1-9d71-d37270cba93f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 03:36:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Midterms: Abdul El-Sayed, Mike Rogers face off for Michigan Senate seat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-midterms-abdul-el-sayed-mike-rogers-face-off-for-michigan-senate-seat</link><description>
With New Hampshire and Georgia staying in Democratic hands, Republicans now look to Michigan for a pickup, where Democrat Abdul El-Sayed is competing with Republican Mike Rogers. France 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports from a Democratic watch party in Detroit.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc5ddf66-d7fa-11f1-a8fe-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b2e393bd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc5ddf66-d7fa-11f1-a8fe-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b2e393bd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77440d5e-d7f9-11f1-a5c2-77086cf0d301</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 02:53:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterm elections: Democrats flip Senate seat in North Carolina</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-us-midterms-democrats-flip-senate-seat-in-north-carolina</link><description>
Democrats have flipped a Senate seat in North Carolina as they try to recapture majorities in Congress and break Republicans’ unified hold on power in Washington. France 24's Florence Villeminot walks us through the US electoral map.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39130d60-d7f8-11f1-8bf4-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-030003-030547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/39130d60-d7f8-11f1-8bf4-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261104-030003-030547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d8798d4-d7f8-11f1-ad11-f16eefb996b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 02:46:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Midterms live: Democrat Roy Cooper flips first Senate seat, follow the results</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">e04273c2-d7ef-11f1-a289-fff07b62cae0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 01:38:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US democracy, Trump fatigue, cost of living are top issues with voters, AP survey finds</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-fatigue-cost-of-living-and-corruption-are-top-issues-with-us-voters-ap-survey-finds</link><description>
Roughly 6 in 10 voters deeply disapprove of US President Donald Trump's presidency, according to an AP survey released Tuesday. About 4 in 10 say the economy is the most important issue while 3 in 10 say the state of US democracy is of primary concern – well above the number that rated crime or immigration as most important.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f173e06-d7d6-11f1-a16f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Vote.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f173e06-d7d6-11f1-a16f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Vote.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bac925aa-d7e0-11f1-bdba-91649190fde7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 23:46:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f173e06-d7d6-11f1-a16f-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/Vote.jpg">© Kristopher Radder/The Brattleboro Reformer via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Historian Timothy Snyder: Trump running US foreign policy 'as though he were an organized criminal'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261103-historian-timothy-snyder-trump-running-us-foreign-policy-as-though-he-were-an-organized-criminal</link><description>
As Americans head to the polls for the midterm elections, François Picard welcomes historian Timothy Snyder, professor at the University of Toronto's Munk School of Global Affairs, for a conversation about the future of American democracy, the growing political influence of technology billionaires and the dangers of a new Gilded Age. Who really holds power in Donald Trump's America: the president or the billionaires surrounding him?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75819288-d7cd-11f1-b8fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-183022-184342-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/75819288-d7cd-11f1-b8fc-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261103-183022-184342-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f54361b0-d7d5-11f1-8978-d3fb20b83668</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 22:28:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Trump tariffs hitting small businesses</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261103-trump-tariffs-hitting-small-businesses</link><description>
As US voters cast their ballots in the midterm elections, the economy remained their top concern. Despite robust headline macroeconomic data, middle-class Americans are growing increasingly frustrated with the rising cost of living. Meanwhile, Donald Trump's tariffs have hit small businesses hard, leading to a significant rise in bankruptcies. Our correspondents met with some business owners.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20d89f90-d7cf-11f1-8f35-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f0deb94c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20d89f90-d7cf-11f1-8f35-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f0deb94c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e9c86dfe-d7cf-11f1-808a-5f6a40722c51</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:45:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Yuka ROYER</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends</link><description>
In tonight's edition, Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the U.S. market after being excluded from the AGOA trade program. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. And  in the DRC's mining capital, Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines... accusing it of poisoning their environment. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/360b5014-d7cb-11f1-a00a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006210-VOD-00023658-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/360b5014-d7cb-11f1-a00a-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/DL00006210-VOD-00023658-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d05b5f42-d7cb-11f1-9e68-df2784793caa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 21:18:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Clarisse FORTUNÉ</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Trump promised a 'Golden Age'. What has he delivered at home?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261103-trump-promised-a-golden-age-what-has-he-delivered-at-home</link><description>
Donald Trump promised Americans a “Golden Age” when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/062b0288-d7c9-11f1-8d33-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/domestic-policy.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1815b358-d7c9-11f1-ad2c-2b007ce09517</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 20:56:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description>
Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? Election Day in the United States with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We’ll track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of Midterms results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump’s second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41f61bb0-d7b8-11f1-95c1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T181429Z-313567485-RC2HGOA1QIDG-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-FLORIDA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41f61bb0-d7b8-11f1-95c1-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-03T181429Z-313567485-RC2HGOA1QIDG-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-FLORIDA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ed90926-d7b7-11f1-8403-23dceba682b2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 19:18:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Midterms live: Voting under way to determine control of Congress and the future of Trump's agenda</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">5e8e6eaa-d7b6-11f1-9345-c9db043f752b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 18:42:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France in focus</category><title>France's dermatology crisis: Patients desperate for appointments</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20261103-france-s-dermatology-crisis-patients-desperate-for-appointments</link><description>
Around 200,000 cases of skin cancer are diagnosed in France every year. Yet as more and more patients seek medical advice, getting an appointment with a dermatologist is becoming increasingly difficult. Half the country's dermatologists are nearing retirement, and only around 100 new specialists are trained up each year. Faced with this growing shortage, some are coming up with innovative solutions. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis and Sonia Baritello report. 
